  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bhutan Economic and Education Support Activity (BEESA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Bhutan):  .USAID provides targeted technical assistance to address priority barriers to Bhutan&apos;s sustainable economic development. As many as 20% of the country&apos;s youth faces unemployment, contributing to sustained, heavy outmigration that threatens the long-term stability of this small mountain nation. In addition, large-scale rural-to-urban internal migration, particularly to Thimphu and Paro, stresses metropolitan social service systems and infrastructure, which are already challenged by the effects of fast growth, frequent earthquakes, and worsening climate change...This mechanism will address key barriers to the growth of economic opportunities within Bhutan to counter outmigration and drive prosperity. BEESA will advance the Royal Government of Bhutan&apos;s (RGoB) strategic shift toward a digital economy by supporting improved secondary school Science, Technology, Engineering, and Mathematics (STEM) laboratories to strengthen the skills of Bhutan&apos;s future workforce. In consultation with the RGoB, USAID may also support Bhutan&apos;s banking system to provide better-suited loan products to small business owners and entrepreneurs, particularly those from vulnerable or marginalized populations. USAID will also explore support to the RGoB&apos;s Thimphu-Paro economic corridor, to include the planning and design of disaster- and climate-resilient productive infrastructure to stimulate private sector economic activity and support social services provision for a growing urban population, in accordance with the priorities of the Bhutanese government. Resource efficient construction techniques and approaches could be promoted to conserve energy and water resources and foster new technologies and employment opportunities. USAID may provide capacity building for government, institutions, and organizations in development planning and management and in locally led climate change adaptation... .</narrative>
  </description>
